# State Machine Rules

- VALID_TRANSITIONS is the single source of truth. Don't fork it.
- Terminal states (`COMPLETE`, `FAILED`, `BLOCKED`, `EXPIRED`) MUST have
  empty transition arrays. Adding outgoing transitions to a terminal state is
  a breaking change requiring an ADR.
- `isToolCallImmutable` MUST return `true` for any ToolCall whose status is
  `approved` or `done`, or whose parent intent is in any post-APPROVED state.
- `computeInvalidatedIds` must traverse the dependency graph breadth-first
  and return the transitive closure including the seeds themselves.
- `topologicalSort` MUST throw on cycle detection — silent partial sorts
  are forbidden.
- Every public function in `state.ts` requires a unit test covering both
  the happy path and at least one invariant-violation path.
